# oracle: fix wall/reflect xlo/xhi EDGE on a fixed boundary with neighbour rebuilds every 20 steps and no check (the
# examples/PACKAGES/shock/nemd setup, cut down): native reflects in post_integrate, before the rebuild and the force
# call, so no atom is lost and the forces never see an atom beyond a wall. The engine reflected in end_of_step and lost
# an atom through the fixed boundary in the nemd equilibration.
# (pair lj/cut, not the nemd lj/cubic: tests/engineRestartPairs takes the first case of each pair style by file name, without its fixes)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map yes sort 0 0
boundary        f p p
lattice         fcc 0.7071067811865475 origin 1.0e-5 1.0e-5 1.0e-5
region          box block 0 6 0 3 0 3 units lattice
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 region box
mass            1 1.0
velocity        all create 3.0 87287
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 20 delay 0 check no
fix             1 all nve
fix             xwalls all wall/reflect xlo EDGE xhi EDGE
timestep        0.0005
thermo_style    custom step atoms temp pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
run             400
